      "kind": "lecture",
      "number": 1,
      "branch": "foundations",
      "title": {
        "en": "What is AI? (+ Syllabus)",
        "zh": "什么是 AI？（+ 课程大纲）"
      },
      "lesson": "lessons/lec01.json",
      "practice": "practice/lec01.json",
      "glossary": "glossary/lec01.json",
      "sectionIds": [
        "s01-ai-means-to-you",
        "s02-ai-umbrella",
        "s03-broad-vs-narrow",
        "s04-russell-norvig-grid",
        "s05-thinking-humanly",
        "s06-turing-test",
        "s07-rationality",
        "s08-thinking-rationally",
        "s09-acting-rationally",
        "s10-course-definition",
        "s11-symbolic-ai",
        "s12-symbolic-weaknesses",
        "s13-machine-learning",
        "s14-ml-strengths-weaknesses",
        "s15-llms",
        "s16-llm-weaknesses",
        "s17-big-table",
        "s18-course-logistics"
      ],
      "oneLiner": {
        "zh": "AI 有很多互相竞争的定义。本课程的定义：AI 是一个研究领域，研究会观察环境、会执行行动的智能体（agent），目标是设计出行为理性的智能体。本课还介绍了三种 AI 方法：符号 AI、机器学习，以及属于机器学习的大语言模型。",
        "en": "There are many competing definitions of AI. In this course, AI is a field of study concerned with agents that observe their environment and perform actions; the goal is to design agents that behave rationally. The lecture also introduces Symbolic AI, Machine Learning and LLMs (a type of ML)."
      },
      "estimatedMinutes": 135,
      "questionCount": 43,
      "termCount": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "lec02",
      "kind": "lecture",
      "number": 2,
      "branch": "symbolic",
      "title": {
        "en": "Algorithms: An Introduction to Algorithmic Thinking",
        "zh": "算法：算法思维入门"
      },
      "lesson": "lessons/lec02.json",
      "practice": "practice/lec02.json",
      "glossary": "glossary/lec02.json",
      "sectionIds": [
        "s01-roadmap",
        "s02-what-is-an-algorithm",
        "s03-precision-evil-genie",
        "s04-programming-language-program",
        "s05-turtle-sequence",
        "s06-first-program-reuse",
        "s07-functions",
        "s08-parameters",
        "s09-abstraction-emergence",
        "s10-loops-definition",
        "s11-loops-robot-example",
        "s12-loop-activities",
        "s13-algorithmic-thinking",
        "s14-algorithms-vs-ai",
        "s15-algorithm-pros-cons",
        "s16-computation-time",
        "s17-counting-executions",
        "s18-exam-review"
      ],
      "oneLiner": {
        "zh": "算法就是一串精确的、按顺序一步步执行、用来达成目标的指令；函数和循环让我们把指令打包复用；一般来说，步骤由程序员写好的不算 AI，程序员只给目标、由电脑自己找步骤的算 AI；而电脑每执行一条指令都要花时间。",
        "en": "An algorithm is a series of precise instructions followed step-by-step, in order, to achieve a goal; functions and loops let us reuse instructions; as a general rule, it is AI when the programmer gives a goal and the computer finds the steps; and every instruction executed costs time."
      },
      "estimatedMinutes": 135,
      "questionCount": 44,
      "termCount": 39
    },
